{% if odoo_version == '16.0' %}
## Odoo 16 has no expression-valued `invisible`/`readonly`/`required`

`invisible="not method_name"` / `readonly="state == 'done'"` is **Odoo 17+**
view syntax. On 16 those attributes accept only `"1"`/`"0"`; conditions go
through `attrs` with a domain:

```xml
<!-- 17+ (fails to LOAD on 16) -->
<field name="method_name" invisible="not method_name"/>
<!-- 16 -->
<field name="method_name" attrs="{'invisible': [('method_name', '=', False)]}"/>
```

The symptom is misleading: a `ParseError: while parsing <file> ... somewhere
inside <record>` ending in `AttributeError: 'ValueError' object has no
attribute 'context'` — nothing names the attribute. Recognise it by an
`invisible=`/`readonly=`/`required=` with a non-`1`/`0` value in the quoted
record. Find them all:

```bash
grep -rPn '\b(invisible|readonly|required|column_invisible)="(?!1")(?!0")[^"]' --include='*.xml' .
```
{% else %}
## Odoo {{ odoo_version.split('.')[0] }} uses expression attributes, `attrs` is gone

`attrs`/`states` were removed in 17.0 — conditions live directly in the
attribute (`invisible="not method_name"`, `readonly="state == 'done'"`). Code
ported from ≤16 that still carries `attrs=` fails view validation.
{% endif %}

## View inheritance selectors: never xpath on `string`

- `<xpath expr="//button[@string='Locations']">` fails the view validator at
  module update — *"View inheritance may not use attribute 'string' as a
  selector"* (translatable, so the match would depend on loading language). The
  registry fails to load until fixed.
- **Anchor an action button on its xmlid reference**:
  `<xpath expr="//button[@name='%(module.action_xmlid)d']">` works — the
  `%(xmlid)d` substitution runs over the whole serialized arch, attribute
  values included. It is the same expression core used to emit the node, so it
  matches by construction, and if core retargets the button the update fails
  loudly instead of silently skipping.
- **An arch test reading `get_view()` cannot see `groups` or `attrs`** —
  postprocessing consumes `groups` and rewrites `attrs` into `modifiers`. To
  pin that a `position="replace"` kept the original gates, read
  `view.get_combined_arch()` (raw inherited arch) or assert on `modifiers`.
- A group grant in such a test can be a no-op when the group is implied by
  `base.group_user` on that database — granting it proves nothing.

## A field's `domain` can't reference a stricter-`groups` field

View validation rejects a field whose `domain` references another field
restricted to a stricter group than itself ("Field 'company_id' used in domain
of field 'payment_term_id' ... is restricted to the group(s) ..."). Fix: make
the referenced field at least as visible — drop its `groups=` on the view node,
or add an ungrouped `<field name="company_id" invisible="1"/>` helper.

Debugging gotcha: during `-u` the real error is buried under a `ParseError` and
then a "cursor already closed" + `KeyError` cascade — do not chase the xmlid
KeyError, it's collateral. Re-run with `--log-handler odoo.tools.convert:DEBUG`
for the true root line. A normal service boot (cached views) loads fine, so
"HTTP 200 but `-u` fails on views" points at strict view re-validation.

## `base.menu_custom` is developer-mode-only

`base.menu_custom` ("Custom" under Settings) is gated by `base.group_no_one`,
active only in developer mode — any menu parented under it silently disappears
in normal mode, for admins too. A menu is visible only if the user passes the
group check on EVERY ancestor. Good parents for a custom tool menu: no parent
(top-level), or `base.menu_administration` (admins only).

Also: `load_menus` is ormcache'd — a separate `-u ... --stop-after-init`
commits menu rows but does NOT invalidate the running server's cache. Restart
the service after a menu change.

## Action `search_default_group_*` overrides the pivot arch's row axis

A `search_default_group_<filter>` context key passed by the action becomes the
pivot's **row** groupby at runtime and overrides the arch's `type="row"` field
(the `type="col"` axis survives). Symptom: the pivot opens grouped the "wrong"
way despite a correct-looking view. Fix: make the action's
`search_default_group_*` match the intended row axis, or drop it. Unit tests
assert generated records, not the rendered groupby — only a browser check
catches this.

## Hiding "New" in the m2m picker dialog

"Add a line" on a m2m opens `SelectCreateDialog`; hiding its "New" button is
NOT `options="{'no_create': True}"` (autocomplete-only). The control path is
the embedded tree's `create` flag:

```xml
<field name="field_ids" options="{'no_open': True}">
    <tree create="false" edit="false">
        <field name="name"/>
    </tree>
</field>
```
